WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.383 --> 00:00:05.243
The map tells you where a region is.

2
00:00:06.043 --> 00:00:07.243
How do you find out what it does?

3
00:00:08.267 --> 00:00:09.527
You need an experiment.

4
00:00:10.427 --> 00:00:12.147
Each kind licenses a different claim.

5
00:00:13.167 --> 00:00:19.147
First, a lesion. A deficit after damage, compared with controls, shows the tissue

6
00:00:19.147 --> 00:00:20.347
contributes to the task.

7
00:00:21.317 --> 00:00:25.417
But damage rarely respects borders, so which part mattered can be unclear.

8
00:00:26.467 --> 00:00:27.807
Second, a recording.

9
00:00:28.867 --> 00:00:32.967
Firing that goes with a choice shows covariation, not that the brain uses it.

10
00:00:33.917 --> 00:00:39.477
Third, imaging. Functional MRI measures blood oxygenation, not spikes.

11
00:00:40.517 --> 00:00:45.677
In anaesthetized macaque visual cortex, it followed local field potentials better

12
00:00:45.677 --> 00:00:51.517
than spiking. Field potentials mostly reflect synaptic and dendritic currents near

13
00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:52.517
the electrode.

14
00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:56.830
So an activation does not mark a region as the seat of anything.

15
00:00:57.883 --> 00:01:00.123
Fourth, stimulation adds activity.

16
00:01:01.123 --> 00:01:03.203
Monkeys judged which way noisy dots moved.

17
00:01:04.217 --> 00:01:09.717
An electrode sat among area MT neurons that all fire most for one direction of

18
00:01:09.717 --> 00:01:11.637
motion, their preferred direction.

19
00:01:12.667 --> 00:01:16.267
On random trials, weak current flowed while the dots were shown.

20
00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:21.760
If the monkey uses these neurons, which way should stimulation push its choices?

21
00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:29.930
Toward the neurons' preferred direction.

22
00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:35.730
In 86 of the 89 experiments with a significant effect, that is what happened.

23
00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:39.470
That shows a causal contribution in this task.

24
00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:44.150
It does not make area MT the seat of motion, or show it is required.

25
00:01:45.233 --> 00:01:48.513
So a lesion shows contribution, not which part mattered.

26
00:01:49.313 --> 00:01:51.693
A recording shows covariation, not use.

27
00:01:52.683 --> 00:01:56.463
Imaging shows where a blood signal goes, not which neural signal.

28
00:01:57.443 --> 00:02:00.963
Stimulation shows contribution, not that the region is required.

29
00:02:02.033 --> 00:02:05.233
Reese and Karnovsky also added something and watched.

30
00:02:06.093 --> 00:02:09.493
But their tracer showed only where it stopped, a different kind of claim.

31
00:02:10.567 --> 00:02:12.707
Claim only what the evidence licenses.
